 - **Ticks**: `update()` runs on the `noctalia.setUpdateInterval` interval (default 1000 ms). `setNeedsFrameTick(true)` delivers `onFrameTick(deltaMs)` every frame while the layer is shown. As for desktop widgets, `deltaMs` arrives as a string-formatted number; use `tonumber`.
 - **Input**: pointer and keyboard input drive controls like in a panel, and keys arrive only while the layer holds keyboard focus (see the `keyboard` manifest key).
 
+## Arrange
+
+`ui.arrange` draws a set of rectangles to scale and lets the user place them by dragging: the arrangement of the displays, for one (requires <PluginApiBadge feature="arrange" />).
+
+```lua
+ui.arrange({
+  key = "displays", width = 520, height = 260,
+  items = {
+    { key = "DP-1", x = 0, y = 0, width = 2560, height = 1440, label = "DP-1", sublabel = "2560x1440", selected = true },
+    { key = "HDMI-A-1", x = 2560, y = 180, width = 1920, height = 1080, label = "HDMI-A-1" },
+  },
+  onSelect = function(key) selected = key; render() end,
+  onMove = function(key, x, y) place(key, tonumber(x), tonumber(y)) end,
+})
+```
+
+- `items` is an array of rectangles. Each has a `key` (a string that names it in the callbacks), `x`, `y`, `width` and `height` in your own layout units (positions may be negative, sizes must be above zero), a `label` drawn centred inside it, an optional smaller `sublabel` under the label, and `selected` (bool), which gives it the highlighted border. Up to 32 are shown. Later ones are drawn over earlier ones.
+- The whole arrangement is scaled by one factor and centred so that it fits inside the control, whose size is `width` and `height` in logical pixels. A text that does not fit inside its rectangle is left out.
+- `onSelect(key)` fires when a rectangle is pressed, before any drag. The pressed rectangle is shown selected at once; render again with `selected` set to keep it so.
+- Dragging a rectangle moves it with the pointer inside the host, with no callbacks on the way. While it moves, its edges snap to the edges of the others when they come within about 10 pixels: side by side (left to right, top to bottom) or aligned (left to left, top to top). A press that does not travel a few pixels is only a select.
+- `onMove(key, x, y)` fires once, on release, with the new position in layout units, rounded to whole numbers and delivered as strings. A handler given as the name of a global instead of a function receives `(key, "x,y")`.
+- After a drop the control keeps showing the dropped position. Like a slider's `value`, `items` is applied only when it changes between renders, so render again with the positions you accepted. To take a move back, render the old positions with a different `revision` (any number): a changed `revision` applies `items` again even when they are the same as before.
+- `items` arriving during a drag are applied, except for the position of the rectangle being dragged, which stays with the pointer.
+
 ## Color picker
 
 `ui.colorPicker` embeds the shell's color picker: a saturation/brightness plane, a hue strip, and text fields, with corners that follow the shell's corner radius setting (requires <PluginApiBadge feature="color-picker" />). To ask for a color in a separate dialog instead, use `noctalia.openColorPicker`.
